The prototype was also designed to test users’ reactions related to stress (analyzed here in terms of increase in arousal responses by the autonomic nervous system). Therefore, it included equipment for measuring the physiological response of participants. We used a Procomp Infiniti 5 (Thought Technology) and Skin Conductance (SC) electrodes to be attached to the index and ring fingers of participants, as well as a plethysmograph sensor for blood volume pulse (BVP) to the medium finger.

